                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Step 1. Start your own CD collection\nStep 2. Buy audiophile grade headphones or speakers (I love my OneOdio A70's!)\n[i]Optional Step[/i] Buy 3.5mm to USB-C DAC Amplifier for clean, crispy notes. (Note: some high-end MOBO's have premium sound included)\nStep 3. Rip CD's to PC (FLAC files are great for versatility without sacrificing audio!)\nStep 4. Organize your music nicely into folders (Windows Media Legacy is useful for naming albums, tracks, ect.)\nStep 5. Make a new folder on Desktop. Copy your favorite albums/tracks to it \nStep 6. Buy a Beat Hazard game (they're all good!)\nStep 7. Load it up. Complete the tutorial \nStep 8. Go to Settings, import your music (Look on your Desktop for that folder you made!)\nStep 9. Compete on Leaderboards for high-score on your favorite songs\nStep 10. Seek out more CD's for your collection and watch it come to life on your shelf as well as PC! \n",
